Riftway CEF patch 0013: GPU information, feature status and hardware acceleration.

Adds the static CefBrowserHost::GetGpuInfo, GetGpuFeatureStatus and
IsHardwareAccelerationEnabled (cef_browser_host_get_gpu_info,
cef_browser_host_get_gpu_feature_status,
cef_browser_host_is_hardware_acceleration_enabled), the client callback
CefGpuInfoCallback and CefBrowserProcessHandler::OnGpuInfoUpdate, as
Electron's app.getGPUInfo, getGPUFeatureStatus, isHardwareAccelerationEnabled
and gpu-info-update. GetGpuInfo enumerates gpu::GPUInfo key for key as
Electron's GPUInfoEnumerator (empty strings dropped, time deltas in
milliseconds, devices in "gpuDevice"). Basic information is collected with
gpu::CollectBasicGraphicsInfo off the UI thread; complete information, on
Windows and macOS, asks GpuDataManagerImpl for the DirectX and video
information and answers on the next GPU info update. Chromium collects the
DirectX information once and sends no update when asked again, so a request
is answered at once when that information is already in, and otherwise after
10 seconds at the latest. Without GPU access the callback gets Electron's
"GPU access not allowed. Reason: <reason>". The feature status is
content::GetFeatureStatus, as chrome://gpu shows it. A
content::GpuDataManagerObserver that CefContext owns from context
initialisation to shutdown reports the updates. BUILD.gn gains //gpu/config.
API at CEF_NEXT (999998): API version 15400 and its hash are unchanged.

Resolves: Riftway docs/DRIFT.md A24, A27.
Base: CEF a03e714 (branch 8037, CEF 154) with 0001-0012. Applies in chromium/src/cef.

